# The parent of every team batch queue (design 0025 §4.3, ADR-0028 decision 5).
#
#   root                       Volcano's own; the scheduler creates it at startup
#   ├── default                Volcano's own; untouched (Kyverno keeps workload namespaces off it)
#   └── adhar-batch            THIS queue: the cluster's batch ceiling
#       └── <org>-<team>-<env> leaves, composed by the Team composition
#
# Only leaves schedule (capacity plugin, enableHierarchy), so no job ever runs in
# this queue. What it does is bound the whole batch tree:
#   capability  no leaf may declare more (the queue webhook refuses it), and the
#               tree together never holds more of the cluster
#   deserved    the webhook refuses a set of leaves whose deserved shares sum past
#               it, so it is the room the prod leaves' guaranteed shares
#               (prodDeservedCPU/Memory in scheduler-descriptor.yaml) have to fit
#               in: floor(ceiling / share) teams, per resource. An adhar-batch
#               queue with no deserved would make every prod leaf QueueRejected.
#
# SEED-TIME TEMPLATE (design 0025 D17, user decision DEC-3, 2026-11-14). The
# ceiling is globalSettings.batch.capacity, or by default 30% of the CPU and 20%
# of the memory of maxWorkers x worker allocatable, measured by `adhar up` from the
# cluster's workers (config.ResolveBatchScheduler) and carried on the platform's
# BuildCustomizationSpec. A platform created before those fields existed renders
# the reference values below (D8 on design §2.2's 10 x 8 vCPU / 16 GiB cluster);
# TestVolcanoRootQueueIsRenderedFromTheCluster pins both renderings.
#
# Wave 2: the scheduler (wave 1) creates `root`, and the queue webhooks
# (admission, wave 0) must be serving, or this write is refused.
# TestVolcanoRootQueueBoundsTheBatchTree pins the shape.
apiVersion: scheduling.volcano.sh/v1beta1
kind: Queue
metadata:
  name: adhar-batch
  annotations:
    argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "2"
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: volcano
    app.kubernetes.io/component: batch-root-queue
    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: adhar
spec:
  parent: root
  capability:
    cpu: '{{ or .BatchCeilingCPU "22" }}'
    memory: '{{ or .BatchCeilingMemory "24Gi" }}'
  deserved:
    cpu: '{{ or .BatchCeilingCPU "22" }}'
    memory: '{{ or .BatchCeilingMemory "24Gi" }}'
